# ----------------------------------------------------------
# Local runtime assets
# ----------------------------------------------------------
#
# Runtime binaries, downloaded models, development virtual
# environments, generated audio samples and third-party
# runtime repositories remain local during development.
#
# Production packaging will include approved runtime assets
# through the installer/build pipeline rather than Git.
# ----------------------------------------------------------

# The whole directory, not a list of subpaths. Building whisper.cpp here
# produces a CMake tree — caches, object files, generated projects, vendored
# ggml sources — several hundred files that the earlier per-subdirectory
# rules did not cover. None of it belongs in the repository, and every path
# under it is either a downloaded model or something a build produced.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash: unanchored, `runtime/` matches a directory
# of that name at any depth, which silently swallowed
# desktop/src-tauri/src/runtime/ — real Rust source. Files already tracked
# there were unaffected, but a new one would never have been added, and
# nothing would have said so.
/runtime/

